ybe we're okay  grazie  we made it to italy oh there's a castle  oh hello  right now we're in italy  we're in the wall city  wow  so cool  we are heading to lonzano and then we're  going to order but right now we are on  hunt for gelato all right we just parked  this one's 4.6 gelato yeah let's go  there yes so it's just back here i think  to gelato  [Music]  here we have ali  hello in our italian abode matthew  wow  beautiful butterflies  here we have nathaniel  and our kitchen with renee roaming as  usual  here's our other little kitchen table  and here is one bedroom this is our  bedroom  very nice very spacious  and  we have bathroom here bathroom here it's  getting dark bedroom here it's too dark  to film oh my gosh here we go here's the  last bedroom so pretty spacious  this is home sweet home for the next  four days yes  meanwhile i'm instagram  we are fully touristing enough right now  but look at that mountain  [Music]  this town is so cool  all right good morning it's the next day  it we woke up at 3 45 a.m  and it's now 4 30 and we're heading back  up to the trailhead  to  hopefully  catch an epic sunrise up at sashaydah  wish us luck we're hoping for some good  conditions golden light it is 3.5 miles  3000 feet elevation gain and it is  freaking cold outside it's like 25  degrees so  yeah it's gonna be a workout and super  chilly but here we go are you stoked  he's so stoked  so cold  it really is  [Music]  hey kitty  hi  how's it going  [Music]  taking a break  [Applause]  okay  see  morendo  so  [Music]  lately i've been struggling to balance  my time between photography and  videography  especially when the light is nice i'm  torn between taking photos and filming  and also whether i should be in the  frame or just focus on the scenery  it's kind of frustrating sometimes being  in front of the camera when i really  just want to be shooting but those  scenes also make it easier to tell a  story so i'm grateful for the times my  friends helped capture m